Girls in India have important rights protected by law.

Education: Girls have the right to free education up to the age set by law.

Health: Girls have the right to healthcare, nutritious food, and a healthy environment.

Equality: The Constitution prohibits discrimination on the basis of gender.

Protection: Laws protect girls from child marriage, violence, trafficking, and exploitation.

Participation: Girls have the right to express their views and take part in school and community life.

Safety: Every girl has the right to live in a safe and secure environment.

Property: Girls can inherit property and have equal legal rights in many family matters.

Privacy: Girls have the right to privacy and protection from unwanted intrusion.

Choice: Girls should have the freedom to make decisions about education and future work.

Awareness and effective implementation of these rights are important so that every girl in India can live with dignity, safety, and opportunity.
